        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>As the top two in the Fifa rankings prepare to meet in New Jersey on Sunday we look at the pointers that may help decide the game</p><p>Slavko Vincic becomes the first Slovene to referee a World Cup final. He oversaw the 2024 Champions League final at Wembley (Real Madrid beat Borussia Dortmund 2-0) as well as Spain’s 2-1 win over France at the 2024 Euros semi-final. The 46-year-old’s first World Cup match was Argentina’s opening loss to Saudi Arabia in 2022. At this tournament, Vincic showed Ecuador’s Piero Hincapié a red card for covering his mouth in the 95th minute against Mexico. He has averaged 2.33 yellow cards per game.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/19/spain-v-argentina-world-cup-final-referee-stats-omens\">Continue reading...</a>"
